{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3443","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3443","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3443\",\"parent_revision\":\"a9c1e8473a06e82955d74645dc6d362323c81780f9548712ed3e2db8a2390145\",\"root_revision\":\"a9c1e8473a06e82955d74645dc6d362323c81780f9548712ed3e2db8a2390145\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA repo-wide sweep of every plugin's runtime files found 200 references that resolve only in this repository. The five plugins with 30 or more are tracked individually. This item covers the remaining seven, which carry 23 between them.\\n\\nAn escape is a path, markdown link, or cross-plugin mention in a plugin's runtime files (skills/ and agents/) that points outside the plugin that ships it. An installed consumer does not have this repository, so the reference resolves for the author alone and silently fails for everyone else.\\n\\nAFFECTED\\n\\n- agentskill-kaizen, 7\\n- scientific-method, 7\\n- fastmcp-creator, 3\\n- orchestrator-discipline, 3\\n- agent-orchestration, 1\\n- perl-development, 1\\n- summarizer, 1\\n\\nREPRODUCTION\\n\\nPer plugin:\\n\\n    uv run plugins/plugin-creator/skills/lint/scripts/audit_runtime_escapes.py \\\\\\n        --plugin-dir plugins/<name>\\n\\nAll plugins at once, with per-line findings grouped by plugin:\\n\\n    uv run plugins/plugin-creator/skills/lint/scripts/audit_runtime_escapes.py --all\\n\\nIMPACT\\n\\nEach escape is an instruction an agent cannot follow once the plugin is installed anywhere but here. The failure is silent: the agent reads a path, finds nothing, and continues without the guidance the reference was meant to supply.\\n\\nCounts this low are usually one or two stray links rather than a systemic pattern, so each of these is likely a small fix. agent-orchestration is worth noting: it was cleaned during the delegation consolidation and is down to a single remaining escape.\\n\\nSCOPE NOTE\\n\\nThese seven are grouped rather than filed individually because a separate item for a single-line finding costs more to triage than to fix. Each plugin is named above with its count, so an owner can still find their own. Split this item if per-plugin ownership matters more than triage cost.\\n\\nSWEEP CONTEXT\\n\\n200 escapes across 12 plugins; 17 of 29 are already clean: bash-development, brainstorming-skill, clang-format, commitlint, conventional-commits, dasel, dot-dash, frustration-analyzer, gitlab-skill, holistic-linting, litellm, llamafile, process-siren, rtfp, twelve-factor-app, verification-gate, xdg-base-directory.\\n\\nThe scanner covers skills/ and agents/ only, so commands/, plugin-root CLAUDE.md, plugin-root references/ and docs/ are unscanned and real escapes live there \u2014 the true numbers are higher.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the rule these violate is documented at plugins/plugin-creator/docs/runtime-environment.md. Remediation is usually one of: move the target inside the plugin, replace a repo path with a URL, or delete a reference that was design-time content in a runtime file.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Repo-wide runtime escape sweep, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"13a26c24c323d7243634ba23f757b1008f2c76c6649f4a08987e502ea7211958\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSAp2A\"}"}